# DOMAIN 4 — CIVIL FRAGMENTATION TRIGGERS

## Purpose of this domain
Detect when pressure + enforcement convert into lived disruption — the point where system strain shows up in schools, services, neighborhoods, and daily coordination for households.

This domain is downstream of Domains 1–3 and conditioned by Domain 2.

---

## 4.1 What belongs (validated)

- Service continuity (schools, transit, healthcare access)
- Local enforcement posture shifts
- Protest-to-policy transitions
- Institutional capacity loss (not rhetoric)
- Community-level disruption with persistence

---

## 4.2 What changed (re-baseline)

Fragmentation now presents as partial failure, not collapse:
- shortened hours  
- inconsistent enforcement  
- backlogs and “temporary” suspensions  
- uneven application across neighborhoods  

So we track durability and spread, not spikes.

---

## 4.3 Triggers

### 🔴 ALERT-ELIGIBLE (strict, proximity-based)

Alert only when disruption is persistent (**≥72 hours**) or spreading.

| Trigger | P | I | O | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Sustained disruption to schools/transport | M | H | H | Attendance, routes, schedules |
| Healthcare access constraints (non-clinical) | M | H | M | Intake, referrals, coverage |
| Local enforcement posture hardening | M | M | M | Curfews, checkpoints, selective enforcement |
| Service rationing or closures | M | M | H | Utilities, offices, aid |
| Court or agency backlogs affecting households | M | H | M | Compounding impact |

**Alert rule:**  
👉 Must be local and persistent or cascading.

---

### 🟡 LOG-ONLY (pattern detection)

| Trigger | P | I | O | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Protests without policy follow-through | H | L | H | Noise unless durable |
| Short-lived service interruptions | M | L | H | Log only |
| Localized incidents without spread | M | L | H | Context |
| NGO / municipal strain signals | M | M | M | Early |

Purpose: trend confirmation, not urgency.

---

### 🔵 SUSPEND / LOW-FOCUS

Deprioritize:
- viral disorder narratives  
- one-off incidents resolved quickly  
- symbolic actions without operational impact  

---

## 4.4 Household Impact Override (Domain 4)

Immediate escalation only if:
- school access is disrupted  
- transportation to school or care is constrained  
- healthcare intake/access is limited  
- agencies critical to household stability stall or close  

---

## 4.5 Plateau rule

Domain 4 enters plateau if:
- services remain continuous  
- enforcement remains consistent  
- disruptions resolve quickly without spread  

Plateau = weekly glance.
